 516 (Aug 11) to 4,265 (Aug 7).\\n*   **Clicks:** Daily clicks were between 22 (Aug 6) and 52 (Aug 8).\\n*   **Conversions:** Daily conversions ranged from 2 (Aug 1, Aug 11, Aug 14) to 6 (Aug 9).\\n*   **Click-Through Rate (CTR):** Mostly around 0.9%, with a peak of 2.5% on August 11th and 2.46% on August 16th.\\n*   **Conversion Rate:** Fluctuated between 8% (Aug 4, Aug 11, Aug 14) and 15% (Aug 9, Aug 10, Aug 13).\\n*   **Return on Ad Spend (ROAS):** Ranged from 6.44 (Aug 9) to 11.83 (Aug 3).\\n*   **Cost Per Click (CPC):** Varied from $0.59 (Aug 8) to $1.40 (Aug 6).\\n*   **Cost Per Acquisition (CPA):** Ranged from $5.14 (Aug 9) to $15.00 (Aug 1, Aug 11, Aug 14).\\n*   **Add-to-Cart Events:** Daily events were between 64 (Aug 16) and 845 (Aug 12).\\n*   **New-to-Brand Conversions:** Ranged from 0 (Aug 1) to 2 (Aug 4, Aug 7, Aug 9, Aug 15).\\n*   **Dwell Time:** Varied significantly from 6 seconds (Aug 10, Aug 18) to 60 seconds (Aug 17).\\n\\n**Anomalies/Trends:**\\n\\n*   **August 11th and 16th** show higher CTRs (2.5% and 2.46% respectively) compared to other days, which are mostly around 0.9%. This could indicate a more engaging ad or better targeting on those specific days, despite lower impressions on August 11th (1,251) and August 16th (1,749).\\n*   **August 9th** had the highest number of conversions (6) and the lowest CPA ($5.14), suggesting a very efficient day for conversions.\\n*   **August 1st, 11th, and 14th** had the highest CPA ($15.00) and lowest conversions (2), indicating less efficient conversion days.\\n*   **Dwell time** shows considerable fluctuation, which might be worth investigating further to understand user engagement patterns. For example, August 17th had a high dwell time of 60 seconds, while August 10th and 18th had very low dwell times of 6 seconds.\\n*   **Video metrics** (starts, plays, completions, completion rate, average watch time) are consistently zero, suggesting that this campaign either does not involve video ads or the video tracking is not capturing data.\",\n        \"ds_text\": null\n    }\n}"